{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:f4cbfc58a683894a66b028420969bb75a35fe4acda1bd3dce0024062c11b2041", "sample_idx": 43, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "\"To access the print version of the article, a link is provided, and for those interested in puzzles, a Sudoku challenge is presented. The rules of the Sudoku are similar to the standard version, with a twist that involves cells contained within grey lines. These cells have numbers that add up to the figures in the corner, providing an exciting and complex puzzle to solve. The goal is to fill in the numbers without repeating any within each shape formed by the grey lines. This unique puzzle offers a fun and challenging experience for those who enjoy problem-solving and logic games.\"\n\n\n \nAddition to the standard Sudoku rules, the numbers in the cells contained within grey lines must add up to the figures in the corner. This means that players need to think strategically and consider the relationships between the numbers in the different cells. The puzzle requires careful planning and attention to detail to ensure that no number is repeated within each shape. By following the rules and using logic, players can work towards completing the puzzle and achieving a sense of accomplishment.\n\n\n \nThe Sudoku puzzle is a great way to challenge the mind and keep the brain active. The rules are simple, yet the puzzle can be complex and require careful thought. The addition of the grey lines and the requirement that the numbers add up to the figures in the corner adds an extra layer of complexity to the puzzle. This makes it a fun and engaging challenge for those who enjoy puzzles and problem-solving.\n\n\n \nFor those who get stuck or want to check their answers, the completed puzzle will be available in next week’s Observer Digital Edition. This provides a convenient way to verify the solution and learn from any mistakes. The Observer Digital Edition is a great resource f